    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184-a2">

                <pb facs="0308" n="210" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg210"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Imperial decree of 26th September.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[From the North China Daily News.]</p>
                <p>Yü Hsien, governor of Shansi, is hereby commanded to resign his post and await
                    further appointment from the Throne. Hsi Liang (Manchu), provincial treasurer
                    of. Hunan, is hereby promoted to be governor of Shansi. [<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—Hsi Liang was one of the first high
                    provincial officials who led troops to “rescue the Empress Dowager,” and is a
                    man very similar in character to the notorious Yü Hsien, whom he now
                        succeeds.—<hi rendition="#small-caps">Translator.</hi>]</p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Imperial, decree.</hi></p>
                <p>Wang Pei-yu, governor of Pekin, is promoted director of the court of sacrificial
                    worship and Ch’en K’nei-lung is appointed governor of Pekin in his stead.</p>
            </div>
